CREATED:20260612T160625Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260612T160625Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_316868519@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261010T053423Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261018T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261018T160000
SUMMARY:The Historic Eastern Beaches! (NEW FOR 2026)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n\\*\\***The Toronto History Walks Yearl
 y Pass is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\
 , email**\n[torontohistorywalks@gmail.com](http://torontohistorywalks@gmai
 l.com%2A%2A/)\n**for more information or for signing up!\\*\\***\n\\*\\* *
 *Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket price when booking your space f
 or this tour! You can e-transfer to the following email at:**\n[torontohis
 torywalks@gmail.com](http://torontohistorywalks@gmail.com%2A%2A/)\n\n**Thi
 s tour is a revised route for 2026.**\n\nThe area was first settled in 179
 4 by the Ashbridge family\, whose name is remembered by the nearby bay and
  park. Their homestead on Queen Street East was well to the west of the ar
 ea currently identified as the Beaches. A later generation of the Ashbridg
 e family rebuilt the family home in 1854 and can be seen on Queen Street E
 ast opposite the TTC barns near Kingston Road.\n\nThe Beaches remained a s
 parely settled community until the end of the 19th century when extension 
 of the Grand Truck Railway\, the draining of the northern parts of Ashbrid
 ges Bay\, and the construction of street car tracks on Queen Street and Ki
 ngston Road\, opened the area to settlement.\n\nFrom Sunnyside Amusement P
 ark built in 1922 to Scarboro Beach built in 1906\, it seemed that Toronto
  cornered the market on summertime chills and thrills.\n\nWe had 5 major a
 musement parks along our waterfront\, and two smaller parks\, Victoria Par
 k and Munro Park\, virtually unknown to Torontonians today\, but extremely
  popular summertime places\, years ago as pleasure parks.\n\nThis walking 
 tour is for all walking levels and fitness skills. Please dress for the se
 ason and bring water. And remember to bring your love of history.\n\nIt be
 gins outside the Beaches Branch of the Toronto Public Library at Queen Str
 eet East\, and Lee Avenue adjacent to Kew Gardens. The tour ends where we 
 started\, back at the library.\n\nThis tour has a ticket price of $15.00 p
 er person.\n\n\\*\\* **Please note: Please e-transfer the ticket price whe
 n booking your space for this tour! You can e-transfer to the following em
 ail at:**\n[torontohistorywalks@gmail.com](http://torontohistorywalks@gmai
 l.com%2A%2A/)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/316868
 519/
