BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: History of Parkdale
UID:event_315411604@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261010T053423Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T140000
SUMMARY:Lost Libraries of the Ancient World (LECTURES - 5TH ANNIVERSARY SP
 ECIAL)
DESCRIPTION:Toronto History Walks\n**The Toronto History Walks Explorer Pa
 ss is available. Get it now for $125.00 for 1 year of unlimited tours\, em
 ail**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**\n**for more information or for si
 gning up!**\n\n**The location of this Lecture might change in the next few
  months so stay tuned for more information regarding the venue! As of now 
 the location will still be Old City Hall at the northeast corner of Queen 
 Street West and Bay Street until further notice.**\n\nWe have an amazing "
 Lecture on the Go" series for 2026/2027. New topics and fascinating storie
 s abound! Join me\, and uncover the world and keep active\, warm and cool 
 during the winter and summer months!\n\nI started this walking classroom w
 hen we were under that horrible cloud called Covid. This series was popula
 r and helped people get back into society and life. The first Lecture on t
 he Go was **Walking North America** and that was in October of 2021. Hard 
 to believe it's been 5 years of lectures. So I wanted to do something spec
 ial to celebrate 5 years of exploration.\n\nThe "Lecture on the Go" Series
  is open to members who have purchased the YEARLY MEMBERSHIP PASS\, it's f
 ree for those members. If you wish to attend a lecture and you are not a y
 early pass member then the price **per** lecture is $20.00.\n\nLet's get s
 tarted.\n\nWhat if some of humanity's greatest discoveries were made thous
 ands of years ago\, and then lost forever?\n\nWhat if entire histories\, s
 cientific breakthroughs\, literary masterpieces\, and eyewitness accounts 
 of the ancient world once existed\, only to disappear into the flames of w
 ar\, and the collapse of civilizations?\n\nJoin me for a fascinating journ
 ey into the world's lost libraries\, from the legendary Library of Alexand
 ria to the vanished collections of ancient empires whose treasures may be 
 lost forever.\n\nAt the heart\, stands the Library of Alexandria\, the mos
 t famous library in history. Founded over two thousand years ago\, it soug
 ht to gather all the knowledge of the known world. Scholars from across th
 e Mediterranean came to study astronomy\, mathematics\, geography\, medici
 ne\, philosophy\, and literature. Yet one of history's greatest mysteries 
 remains: what happened to this remarkable institution\, and what priceless
  knowledge disappeared with it?\n\nWas it destroyed in a single catastroph
 e\, or did it slowly fade away over centuries from neglect?\n\nBeyond Alex
 andria\, we will explore a forgotten world of lost libraries and vanished 
 collections stretching from Mesopotamia and ancient Egypt to medieval Euro
 pe\, Baghdad\, and China. Discover the remarkable stories of librarians\, 
 scholars\, explorers\, and rulers who dedicated their lives to preserving 
 knowledge.\n\nWe will encounter lost books\, missing histories\, ancient s
 cientific works\, and literary treasures that survive today only as fragme
 nts.\nThis lecture is an exploration of one of history's most compelling q
 uestions: What have we forgotten?\n\nAnd how libraries shaped civilization
  and why their loss continues to fascinate us centuries later. Whether you
  are a lover of history\, literature\, archaeology\, or simply enjoy a goo
 d mystery\, this special Lecture on the Go will leave you wondering. What 
 secrets of the past may still lie hidden\, just waiting to be rediscovered
 ? Fascinating indeed!\n\nUpcoming topics in the 2026 series:\n\n\\*Philoso
 phy 1: Great Minds of the Western World: Goethe to Kant! - (2027)\n\\*Phil
 osophy 2: Great Minds of the Eastern\nWorld: Chuang Tzu to Dalai Lama - (2
 027)\nLegacy of Triangle: How a New York Factory Scandal changed North Ame
 rica - (September 2027)\n\nSo book your plans now!\n\nThis event is for al
 l levels and walkers\, there are a few steps here and there to navigate\, 
 but mostly on one level. This event in a non-walking event.\n\nThe lecture
  begins on the steps of Old City Hall at the northeast corner of Bay Stree
 t and Queen Street West\, and\nhas a ticket price of $20.00 per person\, b
 ut **free with the yearly membership pass**.\n\n**Please note: Please e-tr
 ansfer the ticket amount when booking your space for this tour! You can e-
 transfer to the following email at:**\n**torontohistorywalks@gmail.com**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/the-history-of-parkdale/events/315411
 604/
